# Lockverity line-ending policy.
#
# v2.0.3: enforce LF line endings for all Python source. The
# release-validation script (``cd backend; .venv/Scripts/python.exe
# scripts/verify_release.py``) runs ``python -m ruff format --check
# app tests scripts``; ruff's format check is sensitive to CRLF
# line endings. Without this attribute file, a Windows clone with
# the default ``core.autocrlf=true`` checks Python files out with
# CRLF endings, and the format check fails with "196 files would
# be reformatted". Pinning ``*.py text eol=lf`` keeps the
# one-command verification reproducible across platforms.
#
# This file also pins the newline handling for the rest of the
# tracked tree: shell scripts and TOML configs stay LF; Markdown
# and TypeScript stay LF (Windows notepad-friendly CR would also
# work, but the canonical Lockverity form is LF).
* text=auto eol=lf
